    "body": "Thanks @aphillips! Here are my results in various browsers, with ~ indicating that they were in the same group (i.e. could not both be selected at once):\n- Firefox\n  - ① ⑴ ⒈: all separate\n  - À Ａ̀ À à à: À ~ à, À ~ à\n  - Å Å: Å ~ Å (all the same)\n  -  ᾛ ἣι ᾓ:  ᾛ ~ ᾓ \n  - A a: A ~ a\n- Edge\n  - ① ⑴ ⒈: all separate\n  - À Ａ̀ À à à: À ~ Ａ̀ ~ À ~ à ~ à (all the same)\n  - Å Å: Å ~ Å (all the same)\n  -  ᾛ ἣι ᾓ:  ᾛ ~ ᾓ \n  - A a: A ~ a\n- Chrome (same as Firefox)\n  - ① ⑴ ⒈: all separate\n  - À Ａ̀ À à à: À ~ à, À ~ à\n  - Å Å: Å ~ Å (all the same)\n  -  ᾛ ἣι ᾓ:  ᾛ ~ ᾓ \n  - A a: A ~ a\n- Safari Tech Preview (no case folding)\n  - ① ⑴ ⒈: all separate\n  - À Ａ̀ À à à: all separate\n  - Å Å: all separate \n  -  ᾛ ἣι ᾓ: all separate\n  - A a: all separate\n\nDoes the ~ relation given by Edge, or by Chrome/Firefox, match any of the Unicode-defined equivalences?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
