    "updated_at": "2016-08-15T21:33:42Z",
    "body": "OK, cool. Since we have some freedom here to pick between incompatible alternatives, I think the best approach is to take the I18N WG's advice as to which alternative would be best. I assume the I18N WG would prefer Unicode C+F to compatibility caseless? If so, can you tell me the best way to reference that algorithm? I thought we were supposed to go for the [Unicode Standard chapter 3](http://www.unicode.org/versions/Unicode9.0.0/ch03.pdf) section 3.13, but I guess maybe we should refer to CharmodNorm's \"Unicode case-insensitive matching\"?\n\nIt would also be ideal if someone could take on the responsibility of updating https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/blob/master/html/semantics/forms/the-input-element/radio-groupname-case.html, which I presume currently expects compatibility caseless...\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
