    "created_at": "2016-08-16T14:59:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-16T14:59:01Z",
    "body": "I think the only argument for insensitive is legacy compat. But WebKit provides a compelling counterexample.\n\nNote that there's a separate use of \"compatibility caseless\" for image maps, for which I believe WebKit does do some form of case folding...\n\nMaybe the right thing to do here is to see if Chrome could add use counters for scenarios where there are case-insenstive matches (both for radio buttons and image maps). If the counters are very low, we could change the spec to be case sensitive.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
